"ml-en\"><h3>📑 School slides — Slide 01 Lesson01 (16 slides)</h3>\n<p class=\"ghi-chu\">matched by content (deck title ↔ session topic). File: Slide 01_Lesson01.ppt</p></div>\n<div class=\"ml-vi\"><h3>📑 Slide của trường — Slide 01 Lesson01 (16 slide)</h3>\n<p class=\"ghi-chu\">ghép theo nội dung (tên deck ↔ chủ đề buổi). Tệp: Slide 01_Lesson01.ppt</p></div>\n<div class=\"anh-slide\"><img src=\"https://media.cuongthai.com/images/academy/ANM313/flm1/d01/001.webp\" alt=\"ANM313 · Slide 01 Lesson01 · slide 1: Lesson01\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1280\" height=\"720\" /><p class=\"chu-thich\">Slide 01 Lesson01 · slide 1/16</p></div>\n<div class=\"trich-slide\"><p class=\"nhan\">Trên slide · On the slide</p><p>Lesson01<br>GETTING STARTED WITH MAYA<br> WORKING WITH BASIC TOOLS</p></div>\n<div class=\"anh-slide\"><img src=\"https://media.cuongthai.com/images/academy/ANM313/flm1/d01/002.webp\" alt=\"ANM313 · Slide 01 Lesson01 · slide 2: • Introduction to Autodesk Maya\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1280\" height=\"720\" /><p class=\"chu-thich\">Slide 01 Lesson01 · slide 2/16</p></div>\n<div class=\"trich-slide\"><p class=\"nhan\">Trên slide · On the slide</p><p>• Introduction to Autodesk Maya<br>• The Maya user interface<br>• Managing Scenes, Files, and Projects<br><br>http://fpt.edu.vn                        11/09/26   2</p></div>\n<div class=\"anh-slide\"><img src=\"https://media.cuongthai.com/images/academy/ANM313/flm1/d01/003.webp\" alt=\"ANM313 · Slide 01 Lesson01 · slide 3: 1. Introduction to Autodesk Maya\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1280\" height=\"720\" /><p class=\"chu-thich\">Slide 01 Lesson01 · slide 3/16</p></div>\n<div class=\"trich-slide\"><p class=\"nhan\">Trên slide · On the slide</p><p>1. Introduction to Autodesk Maya<br>• Maya is one of the 3D program developed by AutoDesk, emulates<br>   the objects according to the three-dimensional space.<br>• The application of the program to be used in a number of areas such<br>   as effective medicine, construction, architecture, film, games and. ..<br>• The Maya used for the development of the game (Modelling), the<br>   TV ads program (TVC) and architectural models. It is also used to<br>   create the film and virtual reality effects (VFX).<br><br>http://fpt.edu.vn                                              11/09/26     3</p></div>\n<div class=\"anh-slide\"><img src=\"https://media.cuongthai.com/images/academy/ANM313/flm1/d01/004.webp\" alt=\"ANM313 · Slide 01 Lesson01 · slide 4: Model\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1280\" height=\"720\" /><p class=\"chu-thich\">Slide 01 Lesson01 · slide 4/16</p></div>\n<div class=\"trich-slide\"><p class=\"nhan\">Trên slide · On the slide</p><p>Model<br><br>http://fpt.edu.vn   11/09/26   4</p></div>\n<div class=\"anh-slide\"><img src=\"https://media.cuongthai.com/images/academy/ANM313/flm1/d01/005.webp\" alt=\"ANM313 · Slide 01 Lesson01 · slide 5: Animation\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1280\" height=\"720\" /><p class=\"chu-thich\">Slide 01 Lesson01 · slide 5/16</p></div>\n<div class=\"trich-slide\"><p class=\"nhan\">Trên slide · On the slide</p><p>Animation<br><br>http://fpt.edu.vn   11/09/26   5</p></div>\n<div class=\"anh-slide\"><img src=\"https://media.cuongthai.com/images/academy/ANM313/flm1/d01/006.webp\" alt=\"ANM313 · Slide 01 Lesson01 · slide 6: Texture – lighting – Render\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1280\" height=\"720\" /><p class=\"chu-thich\">Slide 01 Lesson01 · slide 6/16</p></div>\n<div class=\"trich-slide\"><p class=\"nhan\">Trên slide · On the slide</p><p>Texture – lighting – Render<br><br>http://fpt.edu.vn             11/09/26   6</p></div>\n<div class=\"anh-slide\"><img src=\"https://media.cuongthai.com/images/academy/ANM313/flm1/d01/007.webp\" alt=\"ANM313 · Slide 01 Lesson01 · slide 7: 2. The Maya user interface\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1280\" height=\"720\" /><p class=\"chu-thich\">Slide 01 Lesson01 · slide 7/16</p></div>\n<div class=\"trich-slide\"><p class=\"nhan\">Trên slide · On the slide</p><p>2. The Maya user interface<br><br>http://fpt.edu.vn            11/09/26   7</p></div>\n<div class=\"anh-slide\"><img src=\"https://media.cuongthai.com/images/academy/ANM313/flm1/d01/008.webp\" alt=\"ANM313 · Slide 01 Lesson01 · slide 8: 2. Menu Sets\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1280\" height=\"720\" /><p class=\"chu-thich\">Slide 01 Lesson01 · slide 8/16</p></div>\n<div class=\"trich-slide\"><p class=\"nhan\">Trên slide · On the slide</p><p>2. Menu Sets<br><br>To switch between menu sets, use the drop-down menu in the Status<br>Line, or use hotkeys. The default hotkeys are:<br><br>http://fpt.edu.vn                                         11/09/26   8</p></div>\n<div class=\"anh-slide\"><img src=\"https://media.cuongthai.com/images/academy/ANM313/flm1/d01/009.webp\" alt=\"ANM313 · Slide 01 Lesson01 · slide 9: 2. Menu Sets\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1280\" height=\"720\" /><p class=\"chu-thich\">Slide 01 Lesson01 · slide 9/16</p></div>\n<div class=\"trich-slide\"><p class=\"nhan\">Trên slide · On the slide</p><p>2. Menu Sets<br>• F2 (Modeling)<br>• F3 (Rigging)<br>• F4 (Animation)<br>• F5 (FX)<br>• F6 ( Rendering)<br><br>http://fpt.edu.vn   11/09/26   9</p></div>\n<div class=\"anh-slide\"><img src=\"https://media.cuongthai.com/images/academy/ANM313/flm1/d01/010.webp\" alt=\"ANM313 · Slide 01 Lesson01 · slide 10: 2. Menu Sets\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1280\" height=\"720\" /><p class=\"chu-thich\">Slide 01 Lesson01 · slide 10/16</p></div>\n<div class=\"trich-slide\"><p class=\"nhan\">Trên slide · On the slide</p><p>2. Menu Sets<br>• Menu sets divide the type of menus available into categories: Modelling,<br>  Rigging, Animation, FX, and Rendering. Think of these as context<br>  sensitive menus. If you're animating then you see the 'Animation' menu<br>  set appear. This will customise the available tools so that you only see<br>  what you need. The remaining menus change depending on the menu<br>  set you choose.<br>• You can display menus as separate windows. This is helpful when<br>  you use a menu repeatedly. Pull down the menu and click the tear-<br>  off line at the top. Tear-off menus always display on top.<br><br>http://fpt.edu.vn                                               11/09/26     10</p></div>\n<div class=\"anh-slide\"><img src=\"https://media.cuongthai.com/images/academy/ANM313/flm1/d01/011.webp\" alt=\"ANM313 · Slide 01 Lesson01 · slide 11: 2. Menu Sets\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1280\" height=\"720\" /><p class=\"chu-thich\">Slide 01 Lesson01 · slide 11/16</p></div>\n<div class=\"trich-slide\"><p class=\"nhan\">Trên slide · On the slide</p><p>2. Menu Sets<br><br>http://fpt.edu.vn   11/09/26   11</p></div>\n<div class=\"anh-slide\"><img src=\"https://media.cuongthai.com/images/academy/ANM313/flm1/d01/012.webp\" alt=\"ANM313 · Slide 01 Lesson01 · slide 12: 3. Managing Scenes, Files, and Projects\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1280\" height=\"720\" /><p class=\"chu-thich\">Slide 01 Lesson01 · slide 12/16</p></div>\n<div class=\"trich-slide\"><p class=\"nhan\">Trên slide · On the slide</p><p>3. Managing Scenes, Files, and Projects<br>• Set a Project in Maya<br>• Managing Scenes, Files, and Projects<br>• Set a Project in Maya<br>• You can see where files are sourced/saved in the project directory using<br>   the Project Window or the workspace.mel file. Here are the most common:<br>• Loaded and saved files: &lt;project&gt;\\scenes<br>• Textures: &lt;project&gt;\\sourceimages<br>• Playblasts: &lt;project&gt;\\movies<br>• Rendered images: &lt;project&gt;\\image<br><br>http://fpt.edu.vn                                                 11/09/26   12</p></div>\n<div class=\"anh-slide\"><img src=\"https://media.cuongthai.com/images/academy/ANM313/flm1/d01/013.webp\" alt=\"ANM313 · Slide 01 Lesson01 · slide 13: Projects and relative paths\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1280\" height=\"720\" /><p class=\"chu-thich\">Slide 01 Lesson01 · slide 13/16</p></div>\n<div class=\"trich-slide\"><p class=\"nhan\">Trên slide · On the slide</p><p>Projects and relative paths<br>• Projects use relative paths to locate files associated with the project. For<br>  example, when you load a texture, Maya looks first in the<br>  project's sourceimages folder. The first time this texture is loaded, the image<br>  name uses this as the relative path labelled sourceimage\\&lt;image file&gt;<br><br>•      This way, you can move the file to any project that has<br>      the sourceimages folder, that is, contains the same structure. This becomes<br>      the relative file path rule. If you load a texture outside of the file path rules,<br>      the path becomes absolute , for example, C:\\textures\\&lt;image file&gt;. You can<br>      read the file path rules in<br><br>http://fpt.edu.vn                                                             11/09/26     13</p></div>\n<div class=\"anh-slide\"><img src=\"https://media.cuongthai.com/images/academy/ANM313/flm1/d01/014.webp\" alt=\"ANM313 · Slide 01 Lesson01 · slide 14: Create a new project\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1280\" height=\"720\" /><p class=\"chu-thich\">Slide 01 Lesson01 · slide 14/16</p></div>\n<div class=\"trich-slide\"><p class=\"nhan\">Trên slide · On the slide</p><p>Create a new project<br>When creating a new project, you can use the default locations and names<br>that Maya generates by default, or you can specify custom ones. You can<br>also create new file rules to specify custom data locations for custom files.<br>See Create custom data locations.<br>To start a new project<br>• Select File &gt; Project Window.<br>• In the Project Window, click New. Maya populates the Project<br>   Window with default project locations and names.<br><br>http://fpt.edu.vn                                                  11/09/26     14</p></div>\n<div class=\"anh-slide\"><img src=\"https://media.cuongthai.com/images/academy/ANM313/flm1/d01/015.webp\" alt=\"ANM313 · Slide 01 Lesson01 · slide 15: • Type the name of your new project in the Current Project text box.\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1280\" height=\"720\" /><p class=\"chu-thich\">Slide 01 Lesson01 · slide 15/16</p></div>\n<div class=\"trich-slide\"><p class=\"nhan\">Trên slide · On the slide</p><p>• Type the name of your new project in the Current Project text box.<br>• Click the browse icon to the right of Location, and then specify a<br>   location for your project directory.<br>This location is known as the project root directory. You can use this<br>location for primary and secondary project locations and any other<br>locations you add to your project.<br><br>http://fpt.edu.vn                                            11/09/26    15</p></div>\n<div class=\"anh-slide\"><img src=\"https://media.cuongthai.com/images/academy/ANM313/flm1/d01/016.webp\" alt=\"ANM313 · Slide 01 Lesson01 · slide 16: • To change the directory of a primary project location, click the browse icon\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1280\" height=\"720\" /><p class=\"chu-thich\">Slide 01 Lesson01 · slide 16/16</p></div>\n<div class=\"trich-slide\"><p class=\"nhan\">Trên slide · On the slide</p><p>• To change the directory of a primary project location, click the browse icon<br>  at the end of its text field, and then specify a new directory. Otherwise,<br>  the Primary Project Locations are added to the specified projects<br>  root Location.<br>• To change the directory of a secondary or translator data location,<br>  select Edit, click the browse icon at the end of its text field, and then specify<br>  a new directory. Otherwise, the Secondary Project Locations are added to the<br>  specified projects root Location.<br>• Click Accept to save your changes and close the Project Window. This<br>  creates the project directories and sub-directories if they don't already exist.<br><br>http://fpt.edu.vn                                                       11/09/26      16</p></div>\n<div class=\"ml-en\"><h3>🔗 Links on these slides — watch/read them</h3></div>\n<div class=\"ml-vi\"><h3>🔗 Link trong slide — xem/đọc thêm</h3></div>\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"http://fpt.edu.vn\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">http://fpt.edu.vn</a></li>\n</ul>\n<div class=\"ml-en\"><div class=\"note-ct\">📝 Detailed lecture and 🎬 video for this session: coming later. For now follow the slides, the materials and the tasks above.</div></div>\n<div class=\"ml-vi\"><div class=\"note-ct\">📝 Bài giảng chi tiết và 🎬 video cho buổi này: sẽ bổ sung sau. Trước mắt học theo slide, tài liệu và nhiệm vụ ở trên.</div></div>"
